    <bpmn:process id="W_W3910" name="W3910. Demand Sensing &amp; Short-Cycle Forecast Adjustment" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Near-term signal (POS, ecommerce, weather, typhoon)
Frequency: Weekly + real-time signals
Volume: Weekly adjustments to 0–4 week horizon
Owner: Demand Planning / Supply
Participants: Demand Planning, Supply Planning (links to VS-02), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Ecommerce (links to VS-10), Logistics (links to VS-06), Insights (links to VS-28.1), Disaster Response (links to VS-69)
Source: workflow W3910 — Demand Sensing &amp; Short-Cycle Forecast Adjustment</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3910_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3910_Lane1" name="Demand Planning">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3910_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3910_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3910_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3910_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3910_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3910_Start3" name="Near-term signal (POS, ecommerce, weather, typhoon)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3910_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3910_Task4" name="Demand Planning sense near-term demand shifts from real-time signals: POS…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Demand Planning sense near-term demand shifts from real-time signals: POS velocity (links to VS-08), ecommerce trend (links to VS-10), weather/typhoon (links to VS-69 — flood-control spikes), local events/construction booms, and competitor stock-outs (links to VS-57)
Responsible (R): Demand Planning / Insights / Store Ops
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP Lead
Duration: Weekly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3910_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3910_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3910_Task5" name="Demand Planning translate sensed shifts into short-cycle forecast adjustments…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Demand Planning translate sensed shifts into short-cycle forecast adjustments (0–4 week horizon) for A-items and event-driven categories, and trigger expedite/rebalancing with Supply/Logistics (links to VS-02/VS-06/VS-74)
Responsible (R): Demand Planning / Supply
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP Lead
Duration: Weekly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3910_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3910_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3910_Task6" name="Demand Planning monitor sensing-accuracy and avoid over-reaction (nervousness)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Demand Planning monitor sensing-accuracy and avoid over-reaction (nervousness), with thresholds for when to adjust vs hold the plan (links to W3911)
Responsible (R): Demand Planning
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP Lead
Duration: Weekly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3910_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3910_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3910_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3910_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
